from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((R/'RESULTS.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
e=lambda v:html.escape(str(v))
def table(headers,rows):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(x)+'</th>' for x in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
def source(ev,idxs):return '<article><p><strong>'+e(ev['locator'])+'</strong> · ordinal '+str(ev['ordinal'])+'</p><p class="raw">'+' '.join('□' if w is None else '<mark>'+e(w)+'</mark>' if i in idxs else e(w) for i,w in enumerate(ev['tokens']))+'</p></article>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · TARGET ORDER · v73</p><h1>Does qokedy precede ol and qol beyond chance controls?</h1><p class="notice"><strong>Primary exact-position test: NOT RUN.</strong> Its frozen engineering power gate failed (7/20 planted examples detected; required 12/20). Original run aborted before manuscript scoring. The separate, unchanged within-line sensitivity below is limited evidence: an F-only point-estimate screen pass, without an exact-position result.</p>'
body+='<h2>Engineering outcome, preserved</h2>'+table(['Mode','Unplanted flags / 20','Planted detections / 20','Frozen mode gate'],[[e(x['mode']),x['null_flags'],x['planted_detections'],'Pass' if x['passes'] else 'FAIL'] for x in d['qualification']['results']])
body+='<p>The sensitivity continuation was frozen separately after that failure. It runs only the mode that passed its own diagnostic, with the original data scope, statistic, seeds, 4,999 shuffles, triad family and original four-panel correction unchanged. The failed primary mode was not tuned, repaired, run or declared qualified. Low planted detection is an engineering sensitivity limitation under that generator; it does not show that manuscript ordering is absent.</p>'
body+='<h2>Within-line sensitivity result</h2><p>Bath section · hand 2 · Currier B · raw P. Original folio f75 excluded, H/F eligible source loci shared, readings separate. Statistic: counts of qokedy → ol/qol minus the corresponding reverse counts.</p>'
rows=[]
for p in d['panels']:
 x=p['tests'][4];rows.append([p['reading'],x['observed'],f'{x["null_mean"]:.3f}',e(x['null_95']),f'{x["p_raw_two_sided"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_triad_family"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_four_panels"]:.4f}'])
body+=table(['Reading','Observed net outgoing','Null mean','Central 95% null range','Raw two-sided p','Triad-selection p','Original four-panel p'],rows)
body+='<p class="notice">H does not pass the full correction. F’s sensitivity point estimate (.044) passes the frozen .05 screen, close to the threshold. It is an F-only sensitivity finding, not a robust shared-reading or exact-position result.</p><p>Finite-shuffle caution: F’s pooled-rank family p=.011 corresponds to 55 of 5,000 calibration rows. These ranked indicators are dependent; a naive binomial confidence interval would be inappropriate. No additional shuffles or outcome-dependent threshold changes were made, and the near-threshold pass is not claimed stable. <a href="MC-CAUTION.json">Calibration caution</a>.</p>'
body+='<h2>Individual edges and all other triad choices</h2><p>All six signed contrasts and both directions were included in the minP family. The ol → qokedy label is negative when qokedy → ol dominates. Neither qokedy constituent pair passes the full correction by itself.</p>'
for p in d['panels']:
 body+='<h3>'+p['reading']+'</h3>'+table(['Signed contrast','Observed','Null mean','Raw two-sided p','Triad family p','Four-panel p'],[[e(x['label']),x['observed'],f'{x["null_mean"]:.3f}',f'{x["p_raw_two_sided"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_triad_family"]:.4f}',f'{x["p_four_panels"]:.4f}'] for x in p['tests']])
body+='<h2>Controls, exclusions and selection limits</h2><p>The sensitivity shuffle preserves every line’s word multiset, endpoints and unknown barriers while rearranging readable interior spans. It controls broad first/interior/last placement, not every exact interior ordinal.</p><p>Exact shedy ___ shedy focal centers are excluded in each arrangement, with no token deletion or gap joining. These target-to-target pairs cannot occur with either member at such a frame center: neither word is shedy. Source counts exactly match the outside-frame v72 comparison.</p><p>The correction covers three unordered target-pair differences and all three outward two-edge differences, in both directions. The original factor four for readings and planned nulls is retained despite the missing primary panels. This does not account for selecting the triad, strata or hypotheses from the broader research history. H/F are alternate readings, not independent replications.</p>'
body+=table(['Reading','Movable word slots','Observed pair slots','Movable pair slots'],[[p['reading'],p['mobility']['movable_slots'],p['mobility']['observed_target_pair_slots'],p['mobility']['movable_target_pair_slots']] for p in d['panels']])
for p in d['panels']:
 tr=p['reading'];o=d['observed'][tr];q=o['qokedy_profile'];known=[ev for ev in q['events'] if ev['right'] not in ['#EDGE','#UNKNOWN']];chosen=[ev for ev in known if ev['right'] in ['ol','qol']]
 body+='<h2>'+tr+' · source counts and exceptions</h2>'+table(['Directed pair','Occurrences'],[[e(k),v] for k,v in p['directed_cells'].items()])
 body+='<p>Of '+str(len(known))+' retained qokedy occurrences with readable right neighbours, '+str(len(chosen))+' are followed by ol/qol and '+str(len(known)-len(chosen))+' by other words. All contexts are retained below. Absence of reverse pairs in this sample is not proof of an obligatory ordering rule.</p><p>Per-folio pooled qokedy net-outgoing contributions: '+e({f:vs[4] for f,vs in o['folio_contrasts'].items()})+'</p>'
 body+='<details open><summary>All target-to-target pair occurrences, including self repetitions and other reverse directions</summary>'+''.join(source(ev,{ev['ordinal']-1,ev['ordinal']}) for ev in o['events'])+'</details>'
 body+='<details><summary>Every retained qokedy context · '+str(len(q['events']))+'</summary>'+''.join(source(ev,{ev['ordinal']-1}) for ev in q['events'])+'</details>'
 body+='<details><summary>Excluded original-frame centers</summary>'+''.join('<h3>'+w+'</h3>'+''.join(source(ev,{ev['ordinal']-1}) for ev in es) for w,es in o['excluded_centers'].items())+'</details>'
body+='<h2>Interpretation</h2><p>The F sensitivity result is compatible with non-random local ordering under that particular shuffle. The unrun primary test leaves exact-position effects unresolved, and H does not pass the retained full correction. No operation, attribute, material, timing, prefix meaning or validated syntax is identified.</p><p><a href="RESULTS.json">All sensitivity outcomes and contexts</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Original frozen protocol</a> · <a href="QUALIFICATION.json">Original failed/passed diagnostics</a> · <a href="SENSITIVITY-PROTOCOL.json">Separate sensitivity continuation</a> · <a href="SENSITIVITY-FREEZE.json">Continuation hashes</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification limits</a> · <a href="../middle-contexts-v72/report.html">Original context comparison</a></p><p>Source fidelity and numerical replay checked separately from browser appearance. Browser visual review not performed.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d);--mark:light-dark(#e6edb7,#526330)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1400px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}mark{background:var(--mark);color:inherit}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>qokedy before ol/qol · v73</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8')
print('Limited sensitivity report written; primary failure remains prominent.')
